# TajStay visual direction

## Direction

- Light base: white / near-white backgrounds (**not** full-page green wall).
- Text: near-black primary, muted secondary via `--text-muted`; on deep-green surfaces use **text-on-brand** (white/light), never gray-on-green.
- **Green** = functional identity (search panels, CTAs, category cards, selected states, icons) — not simultaneous canvas + card + input + nav wash.
- Inside green search blocks: **light inputs** + bright green CTA (placeholders must stay readable).
- Premium but restrained — controlled gold for Owner/premium accents only; no decorative gradients / glassmorphism for their own sake.
- CRM analytics may use amber / blue / red by meaning alongside green.
- Strong hierarchy: title → section → row → meta.
- Mobile-first: full-bleed lists/cards, sticky headers where helpful, safe-area padding; History tabs must not clip.
- Consumer: deep-green bottom nav allowed with light inactive contrast; Admin/Owner: light nav + green active.
- Meaningful motion only (drawer, tab switch, confirmation) — respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Binding screenshot reference: **MOBILE WHITE/GREEN RUNTIME REFERENCE** in `tajstay-master-spec.mdc`.

## Layout patterns (canonical)

- **Profile / Account Center** — full-width hub, not floating narrow card (`profile-center`).
- **History** — tabs via `classify.ts`; card = `HistoryRecordCard`.
- **Bottom nav** — Home · Search · Tours · History · Profile (Favorites inside Profile).
- **Desktop** — max width ~1200px content zones; header unchanged.

## Do not introduce

- Generic AI dashboard layouts.
- Random gradient heroes.
- Duplicate navigation to History or Favorites.
- Dark-only assumptions — app supports theme tokens; default product feel is light + green accent.

## Reference files

- Tokens: `src/styles/tokens.css`, `src/styles/taj-theme.css`
- DS: `src/components/ds/`
- Profile center: `src/styles/profile-center.css`
